  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **No Children** (1 review): Reviewer heard it live for the first time after seven or eight shows; it was the second-to-last song [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Birth of Serpents**: back after 73 archived shows (1320 days) [3]\n- **Cadaver Sniffing Dog**: back after 72 archived shows (1320 days) [3]\n- **Alpha Gelida**: rare: 12 archived performances [3]\n- **An Antidote for Strychnine**: rare: 12 archived performances [3]\n- **Wage Wars Get Rich Die Handsome**: rare: 11 archived performances [3]\n- **Wild Sage**: back after 37 archived shows (423 days) [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tMG2023-06-29** (recommended): source not stated; 21 songs; 103 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Mint Mile appreciation banter & Heel Turn, No Children, applause [1]\n- Reviewer expected this to be the last time seeing Peter play with the band, barring a change in circumstances [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tMG2023-06-29**: taped by me; transferred by me; source: Neumann KM184s FOB > Tascam DR680mkii + CA-14 Omnis On Stage > CA-Ugly 2 Preamp > PCM-A10 [1]",
